abstract: >-
  Code, saved logits of every run, a processed dataset and the analysis outputs for the article
  "Selective Decision-Making for Cross-Domain Fake Review Detection under Uncertainty and Cost Constraints"
  (under review). A cost-derived three-way rule labels a review deceptive, labels it genuine or defers it to a
  human, using temperature-scaled probabilities of RoBERTa and BERT ensembles and of TF-IDF logistic regression
  under leave-one-domain-out transfer. Every table and figure of the article can be reproduced from the saved
  logits on a CPU.
keywords:
  - fake review detection
  - deceptive opinion spam
  - selective prediction
  - reject option
  - cost-sensitive decision
  - domain shift
  - calibration
